# artefacts of running, never of the repo
data/**
!data/**/
!data/**/.gitkeep
artifacts/**
!artifacts/.gitkeep
# the committed out-of-time boundary is a repo artefact, not a run artefact: it is the thing
# that makes this week's number comparable to last week's, so it is version-controlled.
!artifacts/splits/
!artifacts/splits/**
# the feature report is the evidence behind docs/features.md — the timings, and which columns
# are structurally empty on which anchor. Committed for the same reason the data cards are: a
# number in a document that traces to nothing is a number nobody can check.
!artifacts/features/
!artifacts/features/**
# the committed baseline is the reference every later ticket is measured against, and it carries
# the params, the backend and the split digest that produced it. Same reason as the split: a
# baseline that lives only in a README paragraph is a baseline that quietly drifts.
!artifacts/detector/
!artifacts/detector/**
# the decision layer's evidence: the resolved cost model with its rationale, where the bands
# landed on each anchor's amount distribution, how well the score calibrated, and what the policy
# cost against the one it replaced. Committed for the same reason as the baseline — `docs/
# decisions.md` is generated from these files, so every number in it traces to a run.
!artifacts/decisions/
!artifacts/decisions/**
# the transfer results are the evidence behind the anchor decision in ADR 0004: which
# gate each dataset failed and by how much. Committed for the same reason as the split.
!artifacts/transfer/
!artifacts/transfer/**
# the zero-day layer's evidence: five systems on one leave-one-attack-out fold, the blend
# sweep, the commensurability audit of the injected family against its anchor, and the
# batch-independence check. `docs/anomaly.md` is generated from these files, and the result it
# reports is a negative one — which is exactly the kind that has to stay checkable.
!artifacts/anomaly/
!artifacts/anomaly/**
mlruns/
# hydra run dirs (no inline comments here: git treats the whole line as the pattern)
outputs/
multirun/
wandb/

# python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# env + editors
.env
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json

# spike run logs; the artefact under artifacts/ is the record, not the console output
*.log
